  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 120 PM CDT Tue Oct 6 2026\n\nRest of today...Largely quiet conditions are expected today, \napart from some strong wind gusts. The fairly tight pressure \ngradient across the region will continue to bring gusts up to 25 \nto 30 mph to the surface this afternoon and evening before winds \nshift westwards overnight. Will likely still see sufficient gusts \novernight to keep any fog from forming, so the quiet conditions \nwill extend into the end of the work week.\n\nRest of the forecast...\nThursday and Friday afternoon may see a brief period to monitor\nfor fire weather as relative humidity readings are expected to \ndrop towards the lower to middle 30s. Fortunately winds will be\nlower during this period so overall impacts are expected to be low\nat this time.\n\nFrost may make a return to the forecast Friday morning, but \nguidance has become more pessimistic on this occurrence, with \nprobability of dropping below 37 degrees largely limited to a \nsmall section of northeast Wisconsin to around 15%. The changes \nare largely a result of an increase in cloud cover and winds \nshifting southwestwards overnight.\n\nActive weather will remain scarce in the forecast, but a few stray\nshowers may move through the region Friday evening as a weak\nshortwave cross the area. Lack of moisture will largely inhibit\nmuch in the way of measurable moisture for this initial event.\nQuiet weather then largely continues through the weekend as a high\namplitude ridge sets up over eastern CONUS. Expect a strong\nsouthwesterly push of warmer air, which could bring portions of\nthe area back into the upper 70s to lower 80s for a couple of \ndays.",
